  "id": "F",
  "title": "Bootloader serial DFU on a held device",
  "description": "The agent declared serial_dfu. The Backend arms it with dfu_job; the agent fetches, checks and reads the package and says ready, and only then does the Backend relay the bootloader-dfu offer; the application port drops within the arming window, so the socket is kept and nothing is relayed. The agent opens the bootloader's own port and sends the package as HCI packets in SLIP frames (start, init, data, stop; every byte shown), then the application port returns and the agent declares and says hello again on the same socket. The offer's arguments are illustrative; the firmware's update contract is authoritative. The package is synthetic.",
  "link": "companion",
